@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+﻿# UI_UX_README.md
+
+## Purpose
+
+This README explains how to use `CLAUDE.md` as the UI/UX operating guide for this project.
+It also explains how students can choose one preset from `uiux-rules/` and apply it consistently.
+
+Use this when:
+- handing off work to a manager/team
+- asking an AI coding agent to continue UI work
+- verifying design consistency before release
+
+---
+
+## 1) What is the source of truth?
+
+Use these in order:
+1. `CLAUDE.md` (policy + baseline + reproduction checklist)
+2. `frontend/src/styles/global.css` (tokens + shared system)
+3. `frontend/src/styles/vibe.css` (visual layer)
+4. `frontend/src/styles/responsive.css` (accessibility + responsive rules)
+5. `uiux-rules/README.md` + one selected preset file (student style preset)
+
+If there is a conflict, follow the newest baseline in `CLAUDE.md`.
+
+---
+
+## 2) Current design rules (must follow)
+
+- Font family: `Inter`
+- Titles: secondary color (`--color-secondary`)
+- Primary color usage:
+  - CTA buttons
+  - links
+  - title chips/highlight chips
+- Do not use primary as dominant page background fill
+- Keep backgrounds neutral/secondary-tinted
+- Keep button states consistent with the global button system
+
+---
+
+## 3) Student preset flow (choose one)
+
+For student projects and training batches:
+1. Open `uiux-rules/README.md`
+2. Pick one preset only:
+   - `01-enterprise-authority.md`
+   - `02-modern-product.md`
+   - `03-data-dashboard.md`
+   - `04-conversion-landing.md`
+   - `05-accessibility-first.md`
+3. Apply its tokens/components/layout rules across all pages
+4. Do not mix multiple preset files in one app
+5. Validate with the QA checklist below
+
+---
+
+## 4) Required files for exact UI output
+
+For manager handoff, ensure these are present in the branch/patch:
+- `CLAUDE.md`
+- `UI_UX_README.md`
+- `uiux-rules/README.md`
+- selected preset file from `uiux-rules/`
+- `frontend/src/index.tsx`
+- `frontend/src/styles/global.css`
+- `frontend/src/styles/vibe.css`
+- `frontend/src/styles/responsive.css` (if changed)
+- `frontend/src/components/Layout/PublicNavbar.tsx`
+- `frontend/src/components/Layout/PublicLayout.tsx`
+- `frontend/src/components/HeroAICanvas.tsx`
+- `frontend/src/components/SiteInfographicStrip.tsx`
+- `frontend/src/pages/HomePage.tsx`
+- additional pages updated for title color consistency
+
+Important: `vibe.css` is required for the final look.
+
+---
+
+## 5) How to run locally
+
+From repo root:
+```bash
+npm install
+npm run dev:frontend
+```
+Open `http://localhost:3000`.
+
+Build check:
+```bash
+npm run build:frontend
+```
+
+Optional backend run:
+```bash
+npm run dev:backend
+```
+
+If backend is needed, configure `.env` (root) with Stripe and frontend URL:
+- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
+- `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
+- `FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000`
+
+---
+
+## 6) QA checklist (UI/UX)
+
+Before handoff/release:
+
+- Header menu spacing is consistent
+- Solutions dropdown opens below trigger and stays selectable
+- CTA icon is rocket where required
+- Hero contrast is readable on desktop/mobile
+- Primary color appears mainly on CTA/link/chips, not heavy background blocks
+- Buttons have visible hover/focus/disabled states
+- Mobile touch targets are usable
+- No text wrapping issues in key nav items (e.g., Case Studies)
+- `npm run build:frontend` passes
+
+---
+
+## 7) How to use this with an AI agent
+
+Use a direct prompt like:
+
+"Follow `CLAUDE.md` UI/UX baseline. Keep primary only for CTA buttons, links, and title chips. Do a full pass on [page/component], update code, and run frontend build validation."
+
+Student preset version:
+"Apply `uiux-rules/<selected-file>.md` to this project. Keep consistency with `CLAUDE.md` baseline and run build validation."
+
+Then require:
+- file-level changes
+- build result summary
+- explicit list of UX laws improved (consistency, hierarchy, feedback, accessibility)
+
+---
+
+## 8) Recommended manager handoff format
+
+Share all of the following:
+1. Branch name
+2. Commit hash (or patch)
+3. This README + `CLAUDE.md`
+4. Screenshots (desktop + mobile)
+5. Build result output (`npm run build:frontend`)
+
+This gives reproducible implementation, not only visual reference.

