+# Rulebook 01: Enterprise Authority
+
+## Best For
+
+- B2B platforms
+- Executive dashboards
+- Corporate training/consulting websites
+
+## Design Goal
+
+Calm, professional, high-trust interface with clear information hierarchy.
+
+## Tokens
+
+- Primary: `#0E7490` (links + primary CTA)
+- Primary Hover: `#0C637B`
+- Secondary (headings): `#0F172A`
+- Accent: `#334155`
+- Background: `#F8FAFC`
+- Surface: `#FFFFFF`
+- Border: `#CBD5E1`
+- Text: `#111827`
+- Muted Text: `#475569`
+
+## Typography
+
+- Font family: `Inter`
+- `h1`: 2.25rem / 700
+- `h2`: 1.75rem / 700
+- `h3`: 1.25rem / 600
+- Body: 1rem / 1.6
+- Small text: 0.875rem / 1.5
+
+## Buttons
+
+- Primary: solid primary color, high contrast text
+- Secondary: outline neutral or subtle fill
+- Tertiary: text-link style
+- Minimum height: 44px on mobile, 40px desktop minimum
+
+## Layout and Spacing
+
+- Use an 8px spacing scale (`8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64`)
+- Maximum content width: 1200px
+- Cards: 16-24px internal padding
+- Section spacing: 56-80px vertical
+
+## Components
+
+- Nav: simple labels, no decorative overload
+- Cards: light border + subtle shadow
+- Forms: visible labels, strong focus state
+- Tables: stripe or hover, not both heavy
+
+## Motion
+
+- Use subtle transitions (150-220ms)
+- Prefer hover lift <= 2px
+- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
+
+## UX Laws Checklist
+
+- Jakob's Law: familiar nav + form patterns
+- Hick's Law: max 1 primary action per section
+- Fitts's Law: touch-friendly controls
+- Aesthetic-Usability Effect: consistent visual rhythm
+
+## Do / Don't
+
+- Do keep strong heading hierarchy.
+- Do keep CTA language action-oriented.
+- Don't use bright accent backgrounds behind body text.
+- Don't mix 3+ button styles in one component block.

