+# Rulebook 02: Modern Product
+
+## Best For
+
+- SaaS web apps
+- Startup landing + app shells
+- Product-led onboarding flows
+
+## Design Goal
+
+Modern, energetic, clear product UX with strong conversion and onboarding readability.
+
+## Tokens
+
+- Primary: `#2563EB`
+- Primary Hover: `#1D4ED8`
+- Secondary (headings): `#0B1220`
+- Accent: `#7C3AED`
+- Background: `#F8FAFC`
+- Surface: `#FFFFFF`
+- Border: `#DCE3EE`
+- Text: `#0F172A`
+- Muted Text: `#64748B`
+
+## Typography
+
+- Font family: `Inter` or `Manrope`
+- `h1`: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem)
+- `h2`: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 2.25rem)
+- Body: 1rem
+- Lead text: 1.125rem
+
+## Buttons
+
+- Primary: filled, high prominence
+- Secondary: outlined
+- Tertiary: ghost/text
+- Icon buttons only for utility actions
+
+## Layout and Spacing
+
+- 8px spacing system
+- Hero section: one headline, one sub-copy, max two CTAs
+- Cards: rounded 12-16px radius
+- Grid: 12-column with clear breakpoints
+
+## Components
+
+- Hero: bold headline + supportive proof
+- Feature cards: icon + short title + one sentence
+- Pricing: one highlighted plan only
+- Forms: progressive disclosure, low friction
+
+## Motion
+
+- Staggered reveal for lists/cards
+- Button/field transitions: 180-240ms
+- Avoid decorative animation loops on every section
+
+## UX Laws Checklist
+
+- Von Restorff: one visually dominant CTA/plan
+- Hick's Law: keep option count low
+- Goal Gradient: show onboarding progress
+- Miller's Law: chunk info into small groups
+
+## Do / Don't
+
+- Do keep one visual focal point per fold.
+- Do use supporting social proof near CTA.
+- Don't animate everything.
+- Don't place multiple equal-priority CTAs side by side repeatedly.

