+# Rulebook 03: Data Dashboard
+
+## Best For
+
+- Admin panels
+- BI dashboards
+- Operations and analytics platforms
+
+## Design Goal
+
+High information density with fast scanning and low cognitive load.
+
+## Tokens
+
+- Primary: `#0EA5E9` (interactive states)
+- Primary Hover: `#0284C7`
+- Secondary (headings): `#111827`
+- Accent Positive: `#16A34A`
+- Accent Warning: `#D97706`
+- Accent Danger: `#DC2626`
+- Background: `#F3F4F6`
+- Surface: `#FFFFFF`
+- Border: `#D1D5DB`
+- Text: `#111827`
+- Muted Text: `#6B7280`
+
+## Typography
+
+- Font family: `Inter`
+- Dashboard titles: 1.25rem to 1.5rem
+- KPI values: 1.5rem to 2rem
+- Table text: 0.875rem to 0.95rem
+
+## Buttons
+
+- Default size: compact but usable (`40px` minimum)
+- Primary for high-impact actions only
+- Use semantic variants for lifecycle actions (`success`, `warning`, `danger`)
+
+## Layout and Spacing
+
+- Sidebar + topbar shell
+- 8px grid with tighter vertical rhythm
+- Cards grouped by task, not by visual style
+- Keep filters close to affected tables/charts
+
+## Components
+
+- KPI cards: clear label, value, trend
+- Tables: sticky headers for long lists
+- Filters: horizontal row with wrap on small screens
+- Modals: simple, focused, no long forms unless stepped
+
+## Motion
+
+- Minimal animation
+- Use skeleton/loading placeholders for async states
+- Preserve perceived performance
+
+## UX Laws Checklist
+
+- Tesler's Law: handle complexity in system, not user
+- Fitts's Law: larger click targets in row actions
+- Jakob's Law: standard admin interaction patterns
+- Doherty Threshold: fast feedback on actions
+
+## Do / Don't
+
+- Do prioritize readability over visual novelty.
+- Do keep table actions predictable.
+- Don't hide important actions in ambiguous icons only.
+- Don't overload one screen with unrelated widgets.

