+# Rulebook 04: Conversion Landing
+
+## Best For
+
+- Campaign pages
+- Program/course landing pages
+- Lead generation funnels
+
+## Design Goal
+
+Maximize clarity and conversion with strong story flow and clear CTA hierarchy.
+
+## Tokens
+
+- Primary: `#0EA5A4` (CTA emphasis)
+- Primary Hover: `#0B8D8D`
+- Secondary (headings): `#111827`
+- Accent: `#374151`
+- Background: `#F9FAFB`
+- Surface: `#FFFFFF`
+- Border: `#E5E7EB`
+- Text: `#111827`
+- Muted Text: `#4B5563`
+
+## Page Structure
+
+1. Hero (problem + promise + CTA)
+2. Trust proof (logos/stats/testimonials)
+3. Value propositions
+4. Process timeline
+5. FAQ
+6. Final CTA
+
+## Buttons
+
+- Primary CTA appears once per major section
+- Secondary CTA optional and lower visual priority
+- Use action verbs: `Get`, `Start`, `Book`, `Download`
+
+## Layout and Spacing
+
+- Max content width: 1100-1200px
+- Avoid long paragraphs; 2-3 lines preferred
+- Use section dividers and visual rhythm
+
+## Components
+
+- Trust chips and KPI badges near first CTA
+- Comparison cards for alternatives
+- Lead form with minimum required fields
+- Sticky or repeated CTA for long pages
+
+## Motion
+
+- Hero and card reveals only
+- CTA hover/press feedback mandatory
+- Keep animation subtle and meaningful
+
+## UX Laws Checklist
+
+- Goal Gradient: small steps to reduce friction
+- Zeigarnik Effect: keep user progressing (partial completion cues)
+- Hick's Law: one dominant CTA path
+- Serial Position: strong first and final section messaging
+
+## Do / Don't
+
+- Do keep CTA copy specific to outcome.
+- Do keep above-the-fold concise.
+- Don't ask unnecessary form fields early.
+- Don't use equal visual weight for all actions.

