+# Rulebook 05: Accessibility First
+
+## Best For
+
+- Public-sector or education products
+- Inclusive products with broad audience needs
+- Any project targeting strict WCAG compliance
+
+## Design Goal
+
+Maximum readability, keyboard usability, and robust contrast with clear interaction feedback.
+
+## Accessibility Target
+
+- WCAG 2.1 AA minimum (AAA where practical)
+
+## Tokens
+
+- Primary: `#005FCC`
+- Primary Hover: `#0047A3`
+- Secondary (headings): `#111111`
+- Background: `#FFFFFF`
+- Surface: `#F7F7F7`
+- Border: `#B8B8B8`
+- Text: `#111111`
+- Muted Text: `#444444`
+- Error: `#B00020`
+- Success: `#146C2E`
+
+## Typography
+
+- Font family: `Inter`, `Arial`, or system sans fallback
+- Base size: 16px minimum
+- Line-height: 1.5-1.7
+- Never rely on color alone for meaning
+
+## Buttons and Inputs
+
+- Min target size: 44x44px
+- Focus-visible: clear 3px outline, not removed
+- Disabled controls must still be legible
+- Form errors must include text + semantic role
+
+## Interaction Rules
+
+- Full keyboard navigation support
+- Logical tab order
+- Escape closes modals/dropdowns
+- `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` for toggle elements
+
+## Content Rules
+
+- One `h1` per page
+- Semantic heading order
+- Alt text for meaningful images
+- Descriptive link text (avoid \"click here\")
+
+## Motion Rules
+
+- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
+- Avoid autoplay loops that distract from content
+
+## UX Laws Checklist
+
+- Fitts's Law: large actionable controls
+- Jakob's Law: familiar components and behavior
+- Cognitive Load: clear structure and chunking
+- Error Prevention: validate early and clearly
+
+## Do / Don't
+
+- Do test keyboard-only flows.
+- Do test with zoom at 200%.
+- Don't hide focus states.
+- Don't use low-contrast placeholder text as label replacement.

