+# UI/UX Rulebooks (Student Pack)
+
+This folder contains multiple UI/UX rulebook options. Students can choose one style system and apply it to their project.
+
+## Quick Start
+
+1. Pick one rulebook from the list below.
+2. Copy its design tokens and component rules into your project style system.
+3. Apply rules consistently across pages (do not mix rulebooks in one app).
+4. Run the checklist in the selected rulebook.
+
+## Rulebook Options
+
+- [01-enterprise-authority.md](./01-enterprise-authority.md)
+  - Clean, trustworthy, executive-focused. Best for B2B, education, consulting, enterprise tools.
+- [02-modern-product.md](./02-modern-product.md)
+  - Friendly, modern SaaS look with clear conversion structure.
+- [03-data-dashboard.md](./03-data-dashboard.md)
+  - Dense information layout, strong scanning patterns, dashboard-first UX.
+- [04-conversion-landing.md](./04-conversion-landing.md)
+  - Marketing and lead-generation pages with strong CTA hierarchy.
+- [05-accessibility-first.md](./05-accessibility-first.md)
+  - Strict WCAG-first system for high readability and inclusive interaction.
+
+## Recommended Usage Pattern
+
+- Choose one primary button style and use it for primary actions only.
+- Keep heading hierarchy consistent (`h1 > h2 > h3` with stable spacing).
+- Define a spacing scale and apply it everywhere.
+- Keep at least one UX law checkpoint before final submission:
+  - visual hierarchy
+  - Hick's Law (simplify choices)
+  - Fitts's Law (click target size)
+  - Jakob's Law (pattern consistency)
+
+## AI Prompt You Can Reuse
+
+Use this prompt with coding assistants:
+
+```txt
+Apply uiux-rules/<selected-file>.md to this project.
+Create/adjust design tokens, typography scale, button hierarchy, card system, form styles, spacing, and states.
+Keep implementation consistent across all pages.
+Run build/test checks and report changed files with a UX-law checklist.
+```
